Aaron wrote:
>
> I don't see why people are so afraid of being crowned, if you find a /
> oEnlightenment or ?oE, you know when its safe to pray, and I've never
> been crowned before I can handle most of what the game throws my way
> (I've prayed twice post crowning, during my ascension game. Once for
> holy water, once for sliming). The benifits seem to outweight the
> longer timeout imo (FoD for wizards, nice weapons for everyone else)
> Good luck!

If you use sacrifests for the benefits they offer getting crowned gets
in the way. Because the prayer timeout is higher the benefits start
later in either of the main methods.

Doing an offer-only sacrifest for artifacts starts faster without being
crowned but otherwise makes little difference. It continues to be
dominated by the number of existing artifacts in the game.

Doing a prayer-loop sacrifest for spellbooks and protection points the
cost after getting crowned gets paid at every pass through the loop so
it is much higher.  It's worth carefully tuning luck to prevent crowning
(farm co-aligned unicorns, hoard mirrors).

I often altar camp if the mine town shrine is co-aligned.  Sometimes I
even kill the priest on the way back up (war horses are nice on the way
back up as they will kill the priest for you) to altar camp.  Or I altar
camp at an altar on the main dungeon.  Either way as long as I have an
artifact of choice I take crowning as a sign that it is time to resume
exploration and stop altar camping.  For lawful and chaotic the crowning
artifact is on my list of artifacts of choice.

For a wizard I my do a prayer-loop sacrifest to get a +FoD then get
crowned for Stormy as my second artifact. Having Magicbane as a primary
wield and Stormbringer as a secondary wield I'll lose interest in any
other gift artifact.

But folks who depend on prayer to get them out of dangerous situations
the increased prayer timeout of getting crowned is very expensive.


